---
import './operations.css';
---
<figure class="ops-figure" data-ops-rollout>
 <figcaption><span>Figure 4</span> Keep the way back valid</figcaption>
 <div class="ops-scene">
  <div class="rollout-heading" data-live><b data-phase>All traffic uses v1</b><small>20 dots represent 100 card requests per interval</small></div>
  <div class="traffic" aria-hidden="true"><div class="lane"><b>v1 readers</b></div><div class="lane"><b>v2 readers</b></div>{Array.from({length:20},(_,i)=><i data-dot={i}></i>)}</div>
  <div class="namespace-grid" data-live>
   <div data-space="old"><b>v1 namespace</b><span data-old>100% traffic · revision 1</span><div class="residents" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=><i data-old-card={i}></i>)}</div><small data-old-state>Useful copies retained</small></div>
   <div data-space="new"><b>v2 namespace</b><span data-new>0% traffic · empty</span><div class="residents" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=><i data-new-card={i}></i>)}</div><small data-new-state>Separate format, separate keys</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="budgets" data-live>
   <div><b data-memory>Space: 6 of 16 units</b><div class="meter"><i data-memory-bar></i></div><small>One block represents a group of useful entries.</small></div>
   <div><b data-work>Source: 10 of 30 starts allowed</b><div class="meter"><i data-work-bar></i></div><small data-rejected>All requests finish in this illustration.</small></div>
  </div>
  <p class="ops-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The old application and its cache format agree.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="ops-controls"><label>During the rollback window <select data-case><option value="both">Keep invalidating both formats</option><option value="new-only">Stop invalidating v1</option></select></label><div class="ops-buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 7</span></div><div class="ops-hold" data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <p class="ops-caption">Invented operating intervals, not a Redis simulation or measured throughput. Every interval contains 100 requests; a warm namespace answers 90% of its requests. The 30-start source allowance covers demand and warm-up together. The space units stand for measured groups of entries in a real rollout; they are not bytes or Redis allocation sizes.</p>
 <details><summary>Rollout as text</summary><ol><li>v1 serves all traffic, using six space units and ten source reads.</li><li>A cold v2 receives ten requests. All ten miss, alongside nine v1 misses: nineteen source reads.</li><li>v2 becomes useful. Demand source reads return to ten.</li><li>After targeted preparation, v2 takes half the traffic. Ten demand reads and five warm-up reads share the allowance. Both namespaces occupy twelve units.</li><li>v2 takes all traffic. v1 remains eligible for rollback only while its freshness rules still work.</li><li>P7 changes to revision 2. Invalidation reaches both formats, or only v2 in the broken case. The interval illustrates twenty source starts for controlled refills.</li><li>Rollback uses valid v1 entries in the first case. In the broken case, v1 cannot be trusted; treating it as cold creates demand for one hundred reads, of which only thirty are admitted.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-ops-rollout]').forEach(root=>{
 const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case]')!;
 const text=(selector:string,value:string)=>root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=value;
 const rows=[
  {phase:'All traffic uses v1',percent:0,newCards:0,work:10,explain:'The old readers use v1 keys. Ninety hits save ninety source reads; ten misses still need the source.'},
  {phase:'Send 10% to the cold v2',percent:10,newCards:1,work:19,explain:'Two dots move to v2: ten requests. Its empty namespace misses on all ten. Add nine misses from v1: nineteen source reads, inside the thirty-start allowance.'},
  {phase:'Hold at 10% while hits return',percent:10,newCards:2,work:10,explain:'The useful v2 entries now produce hits. Total demand work returns to ten reads. Check latency, errors and answer validity before increasing traffic.'},
  {phase:'Prepare, then move to 50%',percent:50,newCards:6,work:15,explain:'Targeted warming prepares the answers the larger group will need. Five warm-up reads share this interval with ten demand reads. Both formats now occupy twelve space units.'},
  {phase:'v2 takes all traffic',percent:100,newCards:6,work:10,explain:'The old readers have gone, but the rollback window remains open. Keep the old namespace’s invalidation and age rules working while it remains a possible destination.'},
  {phase:'P7 changes to GBP 22.00',percent:100,newCards:6,work:20,explain:'The source commits revision 2. Invalidation reaches both formats. Controlled fills restore useful answers; this interval uses twenty source starts.'},
  {phase:'Roll back the readers',percent:0,newCards:6,work:10,explain:'Traffic moves back to v1. Its format is old, but its product data has stayed current under the same freshness rules. The rollback can reuse its valid entries.'}
 ];
 let previous='';const animations:Animation[]=[];
 const draw=(step:number)=>{
  const row=rows[step],broken=select.value==='new-only',cold=broken&&step===6;
  const changed=step>=5,oldRevision=changed&&!broken?2:1,newRevision=changed?2:1;
  text('[data-phase]',row.phase);text('[data-old]',`${100-row.percent}% traffic · revision ${oldRevision}`);text('[data-new]',`${row.percent}% traffic · ${step?`revision ${newRevision}`:'empty'}`);
  text('[data-old-state]',broken&&changed?'Invalidation stopped · do not trust for rollback':'Freshness rules remain active');
  text('[data-new-state]',step?'New format; same source product':'Separate format, separate keys');
  const space=6+row.newCards,work=cold?30:row.work;
  text('[data-memory]',`Space: ${space} of 16 units`);text('[data-work]',cold?'Source: 100 wanted · 30 admitted':`Source: ${work} of 30 starts allowed`);
  text('[data-rejected]',cold?'70 requests refused; v1 copies are not reusable.':'All requests finish in this illustration.');
  root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-bar]')!.style.width=`${space/16*100}%`;
  root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-work-bar]')!.style.width=`${work/30*100}%`;
  root.querySelector('[data-space="old"]')!.classList.toggle('untrusted',broken&&changed);
  root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-new-card]').forEach((el,i)=>el.style.opacity=i<row.newCards?'1':'0');
  const key=`${select.value}:${step}`;if(key!==previous)animations.splice(0).forEach(a=>a.cancel());
  root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-dot]').forEach((el,i)=>{
   const toNew=i<row.percent/5,top=toNew?105:36;
   const old=el.style.top||'36px';el.style.left=`${8+(i%10)*9}%`;el.style.top=`${top+(i>=10?20:0)}px`;
   el.classList.toggle('refused',cold&&i>=6);
   if(key!==previous&&!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)animations.push(el.animate([{top:old},{top:el.style.top}],{duration:700,delay:i*20,easing:'ease-in-out'}));
  });previous=key;
  text('[data-explanation]',cold?'The old format still decodes, but its invalidation path stopped. Refuse these untrusted copies and rebuild through the source gate. One hundred requests now want reads: thirty are admitted, seventy refused. Pause the rollback and recover gradually.':broken&&step===5?'Only v2 receives the invalidation. It rebuilds revision 2 while the retained v1 copy still says GBP 20.00. The visible space is unchanged; the safe rollback path has disappeared.':row.explain);
 };
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>7,draw});select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
});
</script>
<style>
.rollout-heading b,.rollout-heading small{display:block}.traffic{position:relative;height:150px;margin:.6rem 0}.lane{height:69px;border:1px dashed var(--color-rule-strong);box-sizing:border-box;margin-top:6px;padding:3px 8px;background:var(--color-surface)}.lane b{font-size:.75rem;font-weight:500}.traffic>i{position:absolute;width:12px;height:12px;box-sizing:border-box;border:2px solid var(--teal);border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal)}.traffic>i.refused{background:var(--color-surface);border-color:var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:0}.namespace-grid,.budgets{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem}.namespace-grid>div{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.65rem;background:var(--color-surface)}.namespace-grid b,.namespace-grid span,.namespace-grid small{display:block}.namespace-grid span{font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-mono)}.residents{display:flex;gap:4px;padding:.7rem 0}.residents i{display:block;height:26px;flex:1;border:1px solid var(--teal);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 18%,var(--color-surface));transition:opacity .5s}.untrusted .residents i{border-style:dashed;background:var(--color-surface)}.budgets{margin-top:1rem}.budgets b{display:block;font-size:.8rem}.budgets small{display:block}.meter{height:12px;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface);margin:.4rem 0}.meter i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--teal);transition:width .5s}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.residents i,.meter i{transition:none}}
</style>
